al Access"],"behavior":"User pgustavo requested DS-Replication-Get-Changes extended rights on the domain root object via the GruntHTTP C2 agent, enabling DCSync credential extraction from MORDORDC.","slot":0,"reasoning":"The evidence shows pgustavo requesting DS-Replication-Get-Changes extended rights on the domain root object, which is the specific permission required to perform DCSync attacks. This is credential access via replication API abuse, not rogue DC registration or NTDS file access. The GruntHTTP C2 agent facilitated the privilege escalation needed to make this request.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E014","field":"ProcessName","quote":"C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1021.003","name":"Distributed Component Object Model","parent":"Remote Services","tactics":["Lateral Movement"],"behavior":"GruntHTTP.exe initiated RPC connections to MORDORDC port 135 from WORKSTATION5 as part of lateral movement, loading system DLLs for remote procedure execution.","slot":1,"reasoning":"GruntHTTP.exe loaded RPC-related system DLLs (srvcli.dll, samlib.dll) and initiated connections to port 135 on a remote domain controller, consistent with DCOM-based lateral movement. The DLL loading pattern and RPC port 135 connection indicate preparation for remote procedure execution rather than simple network discovery or SMB file sharing.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E011","field":"ImageLoaded","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\srvcli.dll","ok":true},{"event_id":"E013","field":"ImageLoaded","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\samlib.dll","ok":true},{"event_id":"E018","field":"DestinationPort","quote":"135","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1003.001","name":"LSASS Memory","parent":"OS Credential Dumping","tactics":["Credential Access"],"behavior":"GruntHTTP.exe invoked SeTcbPrivilege and accessed lsass.exe process, indicating attempts to dump credentials or perform privileged operations on the compromised workstation.","slot":2,"reasoning":"GruntHTTP.exe invoked SeTcbPrivilege and accessed lsass.exe with query-limited access, demonstrating the reconnaissance and privilege escalation steps typical of credential dumping attacks targeting LSASS memory. While the access level (0x1000) is lower than a full dump would require, the combination of privilege invocation and LSASS targeting indicates preparation for credential extraction.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E014","field":"PrivilegeList","quote":"SeTcbPrivilege","ok":true},{"event_id":"E016","field":"TargetImage","quote":"C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E016","field":"SourceImage","quote":"C:\\windows\\system32\\lsass.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1}],"unverified":[],"declined":[],"hypotheses":[{"behavior":"User pgustavo requested DS-Replication-Get-Changes extended rights on the domain root object via the GruntHTTP C2 agent, enabling DCSync credential extraction from MORDORDC.","event_ids":["E009","E010","E014","E018"],"keywords":["DCSync","DS-Replication-Get-Changes","directory replication","credential extraction","domain controller"]},{"behavior":"GruntHTTP.exe initiated RPC connections to MORDORDC port 135 from WORKSTATION5 as part of lateral movement, loading system DLLs for remote procedure execution.","event_ids":["E010","E011","E012","E013","E018"],"keywords":["lateral movement","RPC","port 135","Covenant","C2 agent","remote execution"]},{"behavior":"GruntHTTP.exe invoked SeTcbPrivilege and accessed lsass.exe process, indicating attempts to dump credentials or perform privileged operations on the compromised workstation.","event_ids":["E014","E016","E010"],"keywords":["credential dumping","lsass","SeTcbPrivilege","privilege escalation","in-memory access"]}],"retried":[]},"trace":[{"t":2.15,"agent":"hunter","kind":"text","text":"I'll analyze this alert systematically, starting with the triage view and searching for additional context on the most suspicious activities."},{"t":2.15,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"search_events","result":{"matches":22,"events":"<log_events trust=\"untrusted\">\n[E010] +34s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 7 image loaded: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe ImageLoaded=C:\\Windows\\System32\\cabinet.dll Signed=true\n[E011] +34s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 7 image loaded: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe ImageLoaded=C:\\Windows\\System32\\srvcli.dll Signed=true\n[E012] +34s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 7 image loaded: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe ImageLoaded=C:\\Windows\\System32\\fltLib.dll Signed=true\n[E013] +34s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 7 image loaded: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe ImageLoaded=C:\\Windows\\System32\\samlib.dll Signed=true\n[X0025] +34s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 7 image loaded: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe ImageLoaded=C:\\Windows\\System32\\setupapi.dll Signed=true\n[E016] +35s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 10 process accessed (x2): SourceImage=C:\\windows\\system32\\lsass.exe TargetImage=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe GrantedAccess=0x1000 \u27e6query limited information\u27e7\n[E017] +36s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 22 DNS query: Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe QueryName=MORDORDC\n[E018] +36s WORKSTATION5 Sysmon 3 network connection (x2): Image=C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\Desktop\\GruntHTTP.exe User=THESHIRE\\pgustavo Initiated=true DestinationIp=172.18.38.5 DestinationPort=135\n</log_events>"}},{"t":10.99,"agent":"hunter","kind":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the adversary activities. Let me analyze the key behaviors:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **GruntHTTP C2 Agent Execution & Lateral Movement**: The user pgustavo executed GruntHTTP.exe (a Covenant C2 agent) from the Desktop on WORKSTATION5. The agent loaded multiple DLLs (cabinet.dll, srvcli.dll, fltLib.dll, samlib.dll, setupapi.dll) and initiated network connections to the domain controller (MORDORDC) on port 135 (RPC), indicating lateral movement attempts.\n\n2. **Directory Replicat